{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/684630-kindred-detroit-in-your-world-of-darkness","id":684630,"title":"Kindred Detroit in your World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-01T10:59:21-07:00","id":684630,"title":"Kindred Detroit in your World of Darkness","content":"What does it look like in your games? If you ran a game set there, what do you imagine the Domain to be like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T12:53:44-07:00","id":684775,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/07/06/us/detroit-the-path-to-recovery-from-bankruptcy.html?_r=0\" target=\"_blank\">In real life, the city has now emerged from bankruptcy, but is still recovering</a>. For a game, I'd use the horror side of things, not try to reflect the reality of the situation fairly. I'd play up all the negative representations, focusing on the <a href=\"http://www.weather.com/travel/news/modern-ruins-abandoned-detroit-photos-20130715\" target=\"_blank\">modern ruins</a> and general chaos rather than the recovery initiatives.<br /> <br /> I'd borrow a lot from &quot;Forged In Steel&quot;, the Gary, Indiana setting for <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> first and second edition, revisited in the <b>V20</b> adventure <b>Dust To Dust</b>. A dwindling population of local vampires try to hold on, unable to leave, as they watch old industrial and social influences collapse, while new scavengers move in to pick the city's bones clean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T19:00:02-07:00","id":685136,"title":"","content":"One thing I might add to Oxbrow's idea would be that the fall of the city was in no small part due to the power plays and infighting of powerful kindred or factions, each working to undermine the other's position until one day (night) they both woke up to realize there was nothing left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T19:28:16-07:00","id":685149,"title":"","content":"I'm running a game with Kindred groups based in Detroit and Flint and moving into Kalamazoo. It's got a heavy feel of deeply involved and interconnected gang warfare alongside interactions with high powered politics and commerce. I've been trying to pull on things from the past (auto industry boom times, Detroit's gutter bottom years, the Striker family rise). I've used the dissolution of local governments to allow for some vampires to utterly abandon the masquerade, or make a mockery of it. Flint has been controlled by a dense (growing) coterie of vampires for decades now who have pretty much ghouled the entire police, media and government officials. They control the local airport as well and run an internationally popular supernatural brothel. Some younger Kindred broke off and have tried to do the same thing in Detroit, but are having a harder time of it (in other words, making a bit of a mess of it) and have had to lean on some new, less subtle tactics to stay in control and keep the masquerade. <br /> <br /> Michigan is just an awesome state for a WoD setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T22:38:33-07:00","id":685296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/684630-kindred-detroit-in-your-world-of-darkness?p=684775#post684775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/07/06/us/detroit-the-path-to-recovery-from-bankruptcy.html?_r=0\" target=\"_blank\">In real life, the city has now emerged from bankruptcy, but is still recovering</a>. For a game, I'd use the horror side of things, not try to reflect the reality of the situation fairly. I'd play up all the negative representations, focusing on the <a href=\"http://www.weather.com/travel/news/modern-ruins-abandoned-detroit-photos-20130715\" target=\"_blank\">modern ruins</a> and general chaos rather than the recovery initiatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>That being said, downtown Detroit is starting to see a bit of an upswing. Not much mind you but enough to hammer home a south african feel of insecurity and inequality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T00:13:13-07:00","id":685332,"title":"","content":"To preface, I play NWoD as &quot;our world, but everything's worse.&quot; So while I recognize that Detroit is in many ways a city climbing back on its feet, my NWoD version is still very much a hellhole.<br /> <br /> Detroit has a long and troubled racial history. For the kine, the race riots were decades ago and faded from the memories of many, but for the city's Elders, they were yesterday. <br /> <br /> In many cities your Covenant describes one of your primary allegiances, but in Detroit your Clan comes before all else, followed by your Coterie, and in a distant last place, your Covenant.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue are the waning old money and power in the city. White and wealthy, they have effectively self-selected themselves into oblivion - as their Elders failed to adapt to the changing times they grew ever more picky about what candidates were &quot;worthy&quot; of their lineage. Now they remain entrenched in several meaningful places of power within the city, but the power they once enjoyed has mostly withered.<br /> <br /> In order to hold on to power the Ventrue have long relied on the Nosferatu - those lords of Nightmare who were less choosy in those who they Sire, but unable to have the public and political clout that affords the Ventrue their comfortable eternities. The two clans are allies with a long and storied history, but with the collapse in Ventrue power, rifts are beginning to form in their relationship that could easily tear wide open given the right circumstances.<br /> <br /> Mirroring the Ventrue and Nosferatu, the Daeva and Gangrel are friends of convenience - the Daeva ascendant in the artistic and musical underbelly of Detroit, and wielding considerable power through ties to the Entertainment industry, while the Gangrel recruit extensively and almost exclusively from the impoverished and violent gangs within the city. The often close ties between these two groups among the mortals has in turn lead to close ties between the respective Clans, though this too is not without its problems; especially when both lay claim to a single promising candidate. However, as a whole, the real power in the city is this close-knit alliance of two Clans, enjoying a long ascendance since the collapse of the Detroit Economy.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, the Mekhet of the city have carved out their quiet niche in the city, mostly unnoticed by the feuding factions; which is just the way they like it. Their ranks are pulled from the city's academics and those exceptional mortals of distinction passed over by the Ventrue for one imagined flaw or another. Occasionally they step forward to mediate between the Clans when the situation seems like its' about to boil over into all-out war, but for the most part the quiet conflict serves their interests well, as does the slow decay of the city which makes it easy for people to just... slip through the cracks.<br /> <br /> Not all is terrible in the city though - Detroit has a long memory as well and Hunter factions are strong within the City, particularly the Union. Vampires keep their heads down or lose them with respect to the mortals, who are quick to band together to kill a bloodsucker or two... and Devil's Night is a favorite time for the city's vampire slayers to disguise a good-old-fashioned death by fire as just another case of rambunctious teenagers burning down an abandoned building.<br /> <br /> As a final note, as among the mortals, so too does 8-Mile Road serve as a harsh dividing line between the old power of the Ventrue and the ascendant star of the Daeva. Either side of the line has it's own Prince and it's own Laws, leaving visitors to Detroit in a dangerous situation if they arrive without an understanding of the dynamics at work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T04:08:55-07:00","id":685463,"title":"","content":"I'm very interested in this topic; although I've moved my plans for Vampire from Detroit to Atlanta, I still have a myriad of games slated for Detroit. I'd share what I'm doing with it, but I'm a little afraid prospective players may stumble on it. I'm still on the look out or some good inspiration, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T10:37:10-07:00","id":685915,"title":"","content":"Maybe write about it in vague terms?<br /> <br /> I think one of the thoughts that's occurred to me here is that real life Detroit being on the rebound is not actually a bad thing, and represents a great shifting of the paradigm in the city, one the Kindred might try to fight <i>against</i> because Detroit being a semi-abandoned hellhole with the population that it has is actually a pretty good feeding ground for Kindred, and that on the whole, they may be fighting to keep the city worse off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T10:57:12-07:00","id":685954,"title":"","content":"Or if you keep the rebound, play up how the different factions are competing to be the ones controlling and benefiting from it. Rather like an old west boom town where everyone with a gun figures they should be the new boss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T18:59:33-07:00","id":686323,"title":"","content":"If you're wanting to get a feel for the desolation and haunting emptiness of Detroit, I'd highly recommend watching <i>Only Lovers Left Alive. </i>\u200bFunnily enough, it's a movie about vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T21:39:00-07:00","id":686455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/684630-kindred-detroit-in-your-world-of-darkness?p=686323#post686323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're wanting to get a feel for the desolation and haunting emptiness of Detroit, I'd highly recommend watching <i>Only Lovers Left Alive. </i>\u200bFunnily enough, it's a movie about vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may or may not have inspired this question!...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T05:48:39-07:00","id":686883,"title":"","content":"BTW, what is the official version? Is there even one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T10:18:42-07:00","id":687245,"title":"","content":"I believe Detroit is the 'signature city' of Promethean. It is probably mentioned more than once throughout the Vampire line, but here is the Detroit entry from Damnation City.<br /> <br /> 'The automotive production lines still don\u2019t stop in Motor City, even while other industries get outsourced abroad. Still, the factories empty, and the buildings get left behind. The blue-collar population falls into unemployment and discontent. The city is divided by 6 Mile, 7 Mile and 8 Mile Roads into the haves and the have-nots. On the (literal) wrong side of the tracks, the city has the worst crime rate in the United States. Nearly half of Detroit\u2019s people are functionally illiterate.<br /> The Carthian Prefect, still new to the job, sees the opportunities for the undead in a city where the living are lost to decay and crime. Still, this doesn\u2019t explain why so many of the empty buildings that pepper the city\u2019s surface serve as temporary havens for neonate Kindred who only just came here. It\u2019s as if some force is drawing people to Detroit, some of whom have no idea why they are here, only that they had to come.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T23:38:09-07:00","id":694596,"title":"","content":"My Detroit had the Carthians throw out the Lancea Samctum in the 70s. The LS mostly moved to Windsor where they plot their return. I had the Detroit Carthians splinter into a number of factions, mostly crime based. The Purple Gang, Jimmy Hoffa, and the Black Gangster Family all made appearances. The Circle of the Crone was busy recruiting downtown, and had been working to supplant the Caryhians as well. The characters were refugees from Lansing, whose Prince had just made a literal deal with the devil. The sudden presence of five new unaffiliated vampires was going to cause quite a stir for Detroits vampires...but then a bunch of us had kids so those plans stopped. Being an adult is hard lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}